From ca1a388aa69ff99195e84291846a5a9c4f009e90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t5dr <t5dr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:00:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 99/99] Pad bindings: per-player device and button map from
 controls.ini

TEKKEN4_CONTROLS=<path> (else controls.ini in the working directory = the save folder) is read at start and
re-read within ~1 s when it changes. Per player (player1 = port 1, player2 = port 2): device = auto | none |
keyboard | xinput | xinput:0..3 (joined with +), [playerN.pad] XInput bindings and [playerN.keys] keyboard
bindings, TARGET = SOURCE ... per PS2 button (SELECT L3 R3 START UP RIGHT DOWN LEFT L2 R2 L1 R1 TRIANGLE CIRCLE
CROSS SQUARE or the Tekken names 1 2 3 4). A button not listed keeps its fixed default; `none` unbinds it.

ps2_pad_bindings.h (header only) holds the parser, the maps and the live file. ps2_host_pad: readPlayer /
playerPresent (a pinned XInput slot or the next free one, the player's PadMap; the 1 ms tap latch latches in the
terms of the player who reads the slot). ps2_input_latency: sampleKeys (posted keys + GetAsyncKeyState for the
bound virtual keys, left/right shift/ctrl/alt told apart). ps2_pad: readBound (port 0 once a file changes
something, port 1 through Pad.cpp, the keyboard-only netplay device TEKKEN4_NET_PAD=-1). Netplay and rollback
read the local pad through readState, so they send the mapped PS2 button bits as before; the pad packet, the
netplay data format and the game state are untouched.

No file, an empty file, or a file that only says `device = auto` and lists no binding = isDefault(): every
caller keeps its old code (the fixed layout of patches 29/60/31, bit for bit; tools/pad_bindings_test.cpp checks
the table path against a copy of the old code on 200000 random pad samples and 100000 key sets).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
